l-command-135","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"Render an already-written scorecard JSON instead of reading runs. Repeat it to draw a progress section. Conflicts with `--root` and `--metrics`"},"607":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-136","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"`-o`, `--output <FILE>`"},"608":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-137","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"Write the report here instead of to stdout"},"609":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-138","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"`--no-reasoning`"},"610":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-139","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-scorecard","content":"Leave judge reasoning out of the report and out of its embedded JSON"},"611":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-140","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-metrics-file","content":"Each `[[metric]]` selects cases by `*`-wildcard id pattern. Omitting `cases` selects every case."},"612":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-141","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-metrics-file","content":"`check_rate` is passing check results over observed check results, over trials rather than cases: a case passing three of five trials contributes 3/5. `tool_calls_p95` is the 95th percentile of tool calls per trial, compared against a ceiling. `judge_score` is the mean of a judge's `overall` — or of one named criterion — over the latest judgment per trial."},"613":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-142","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"A number whose provenance is gone cannot be compared with last month's, so the scorecard records four identities beside the metrics:"},"614":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-143","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Identity"},"615":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-144","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Where it comes from"},"616":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-145","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"**Target**"},"617":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-146","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"The `(agent, model)` pair each run recorded"},"618":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-147","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"**Skill**"},"619":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-148","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`skill_git_sha` and `skill_dirty` copied from the run, never recomputed from the working tree — and reported only when every run agrees"},"620":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-149","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"**Benchmark**"},"621":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-150","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`sha256` over the metrics file and every file the declared `suites` select (`checks.toml`, `prompts.csv` and every judge prompt file)"},"622":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-151","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"**Judges**"},"623":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-152","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Every distinct `judge_hash` with the model, endpoint and sampling settings that produced it"},"624":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-153","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Three guards refuse a scorecard that would average two different measurements together. Each names the offending values, and each has an override that records itself in the document, so a reader can see the mixing happened:"},"625":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-154","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Refused when"},"626":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-155","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Override"},"627":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-156","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Recorded as"},"628":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-157","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"A `judge_score` metric folds more than one `judge_hash`"},"629":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-158","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`--allow-mixed-judges`"},"630":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-159","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`metrics[].mixed_judges: true`"},"631":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-160","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"The runs under `--root` carry more than one `(agent, model)`"},"632":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-161","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`--allow-mixed-targets`"},"633":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-162","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`metrics[].mixed_targets: true`, no top-level `agent`/`model`"},"634":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-163","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"The same case id is measured by more than one run"},"635":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-164","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`--allow-duplicate-cases`"},"636":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-165","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Every `cases[]` row keeps its own `run_dir`"},"637":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-166","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"`--no-fail` suppresses none of these: it says \"report the numbers rather than gate on them\", not \"the numbers mean something they do not\"."},"638":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-167","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-json-document","content":"`--format json` emits a `fastskill.scorecard/1` document: the identities above, the `metrics` and `totals` the table shows, and a `cases[]` array with one row per `(run, case)` carrying every check result and, per judge, the latest judgment per trial with each criterion's normalised score, answer and **full** reasoning. Nothing in a row is summarised — the run directories get deleted, and this document is what survives them."},"639":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-168","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"`--format html` renders the same document as a page a reader opens months later: identity, the gates and their verdicts, the exclusions above as notes, the judges and their sampling settings, then one table per suite with every case, its checks and its judgments, reasoning folded behind a `<details>` after the first 600 characters."},"640":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-169","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"It is one file. The fonts are embedded, the stylesheet is inline, and the only `<script>` is a `<script type=\"application/json\">` holding the scorecards the page was rendered from — so the page carries its own machine-readable source, and opens with no network. A run directory is linked only when it is still on disk; a link to evidence that was deleted is worse than no link."},"641":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-170","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"Pass `--from` instead to render scorecard JSON that was written earlier — on another machine, or by CI. That mode reads no run directory at all, so it links none."},"642":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-171","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"Two or more `--from` files add a progress section: one chart per metric, ordered by `generated_at`, with the gate drawn as a dashed line and every point where the verdict flipped ringed. Series are keyed by target, so two agents on the same benchmark are two lines. Every input must carry the same non-null `benchmark.sha256` — a chart across two benchmarks plots two different measurements as one trend, and there is no override for it. Mismatched inputs fail with `EVAL_SCORECARD_BENCHMARK_MISMATCH`; a scorecard whose metrics file declared no `suites` has no hash to compare and fails with `EVAL_SCORECARD_NO_BENCHMARK_HASH`."},"643":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-172","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"`--no-reasoning` removes judge reasoning from the tables **and** from the embedded JSON. It is for reports that leave the team that ran them."},"644":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-173","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"**Errored trials.** A trial with outcome `error` still carries check results, because the checks ran, over an empty trace. Every negative expectation and every tool-call ceiling passed there vacuously, so folding them would report an outage as perfect restraint. They are dropped from every rate and counted separately."},"645":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-174","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"**Not-observable checks.** A check whose evidence the backend cannot produce records `passed: false` for older readers. It is excluded rather than counted as a failure."},"646":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-175","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"**Estimated cost.** Only the vendor-reported figure is summed. When no trial reported one, the line reads \"not reported\" rather than `$0.00`."},"647":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-176","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"**Judge errors and excluded trials.** A trial whose judgment errored contributes nothing to a `judge_score` — not a zero — and is counted in `totals.judge_errors`. A trial a gated judge could not judge is counted in `totals.judge_excluded_trials`."},"648":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-177","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"**Advisory judge rows.** A `judge:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."},"649":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-178","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"A case whose every trial errored is named in the output, and a metric that matched nothing **fails the command** even under `--no-fail`: a mistyped case pattern would otherwise make a gate quietly disappear. Check results that no metric claims are named in a warning."},"650":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-179","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#see-also","content":"`project init` for skill layout"},"651":{"id":"/cli-reference/init-comm