e:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."],[1181,"**API Key Issues**: Check `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable"],[2890,"**Audit Trail**: Publishing history is maintained automatically"],[224,"**Authors**: init, validate, eval, and ship skills via the platform."],[2799,"**Automatic rebuilding keeps the index fresh.** After `skill add`, `project install`,\n`skill update`, or `skill remove`, FastSkill\nreindexes automatically (unless `auto_reindex = false` or `--no-reindex`, and only when an\nembedding provider is available), so `resolve` reflects the current skill set."],[227,"**Automation**: `project install --lock` and reproducible installs in CI."],[1198,"**Average skill**: \\~500 tokens"],[1303,"**Behavior**:"],[620,"**Benchmark**"],[2887,"**Blob Storage**: Artifacts are stored securely with checksum verification"],[1970,"**Case-based evals** with `fastskill eval` to test expected behavior against prompts and rubrics"],[1927,"**Cause**: `--yes` was used at a project root without a skills directory.\n**Solution**: add `--skills-dir <path>`, or drop `--yes` to be prompted."],[1926,"**Cause**: a `skill-project.toml` is already present.\n**Solution**: pass `--force` to overwrite it, or remove the file first."],[333,"**Cause**: Another `fastskill` command is currently running and has acquired an exclusive lock on the lock file."],[1929,"**Cause**: the current directory is not writable.\n**Solution**: fix permissions or run in a directory where you have write access."],[345,"**Cause**: The lock file was manually edited incorrectly, interrupted during write, or corrupted by a bug."],[358,"**Cause**: The system cannot determine the standard config directory for your platform."],[1928,"**Cause**: the version (from `--set-version` or `SKILL.md`) is not valid semver.\n**Solution**: use a semver string such as `1.0.0`."],[1924,"**Changing the embedding model invalidates your index.** Vectors from different\nmodels are not comparable — and often not even the same length. After switching\nmodels, run `fastskill index rebuild` before searching, or results will be meaningless."],[2329,"**Check environment readiness**"],[1401,"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."],[366,"**Check permissions**:"],[1873,"**Checks for an existing file**: refuses to overwrite `skill-project.toml` unless `--force` is given."],[2123,"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."],[2699,"**Checks TOML*&#x2A; — the grading rules that score each response. &#x2A;(Optional, but without it there is no real grading signal — see below.)*"],[2540,"**Checks**"],[2888,"**Checksum Verification**: All downloads include SHA256 checksums"],[2863,"**cksum**: SHA256 checksum of the ZIP artifact"],[2296,"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."],[222,"**CLI**: single entry point for installs, checks, search, and evals."],[3130,"**Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`.**"],[369,"**Commit project lock to git**:"],[1189,"**Content**: Metadata and embeddings used by semantic search"],[1192,"**Content**: Per-skill file hashes used to decide which skills changed since the last run"],[1870,"**Context detection**: `project init` detects whether you're in a skill directory or a project root:"],[2995,"**Converts to internal format** for processing by:"],[365,"**Create the directory manually**:"],[720,"**Creates File**: Writes `skill-project.toml` with basic structure and commented examples"],[2327,"**Cursor doesn't see a skill**"],[1907,"**Custom**: any path you pass via `--skills-dir` or the prompt"],[1906,"**Default**: `.claude/skills`"],[1152,"**Default**: Shows a live progress bar with completion percentage (when stdout is a TTY)"],[2095,"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."],[2862,"**deps**: Dependencies (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[711,"**Detects Context**: Determines if you're in a skill directory (with SKILL.md) or a project directory"],[225,"**Developers**: install, list, read, search for what agents load."],[868,"**Development Mode** (with `skill-project.toml`):"],[359,"**Diagnosis**:"],[2331,"**Direct skill discovery** — Cursor reads installed skills from the skills directory, no sync step"],[370,"**Don't commit global lock**:"],[372,"**Don't manually edit lock files** unless you understand the TOML schema"],[2867,"**download\\_url**: URL to download the ZIP artifact"],[2794,"**Embeddings power ranking when available.** With `OPENAI_API_KEY` set (and\n`[tool.fastskill.embedding]` configured), FastSkill ranks skills semantically using the embedding\nindex."],[2544,"**Epoch**"],[357,"**Error**: `Global config directory unavailable: ...`"],[332,"**Error**: `Lock file is held by another process: /path/to/skills.lock`"],[644,"**Errored trials.** A trial with outcome `error` still carries check results, because the checks ran, over an empty trace. Every negative expectation and every tool-call ceiling passed there vacuously, so folding them would report an outage as perfect restraint. They are dropped from every rate and counted separately."],[646,"**Estimated cost.** Only the vendor-reported figure is summed. When no trial reported one, the line reads \"not reported\" rather than `$0.00`."],[2761,"**Example `checks.toml`:**"],[2733,"**Example `suite.csv`** (has both `train` and `selection` rows, plus a held-out `test` row):"],[1781,"**Example output:**"],[448,"**Example output**:"],[1243,"**Example Output**:"],[1308,"**Example Output**:"],[1376,"**Example Output**:"],[1387,"**Example Output**:"],[2871,"**Example:**"],[1397,"**Example**:"],[3032,"**Example**: If skill-project.toml has `version = \"2.0.0\"` but SKILL.md has `version: \"1.0.0\"`, the marketplace.json will use `\"2.0.0\"`. Similarly, if skill-project.toml has `author = \"New Author\"`, it will override the author from SKILL.md. The `name` field always comes from SKILL.md frontmatter for display purposes, as it is not present in skill-project.toml."],[1333,"**Exit codes**:"],[3123,"**Expose read-only.** For a browsable UI or REST view over your skills, run `fastskill server serve`\n**without** `--enable-write`. Every mutation endpoint returns HTTP 403, so an exposed instance\ncannot install, update, delete, reindex, or refresh anything."],[712,"**Extracts Metadata**: If SKILL.md exists, extracts version, description, and author from YAML frontmatter"],[2864,"**features**: Feature flags (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[1061,"**File permissions**: Ensure you have read/write permissions for skill directories."],[1191,"**Format**: JSON"],[1187,"**Format**: SQLite database"],[3125,"**Front an exposed port with an authenticating proxy.** `server serve` enforces no authentication of its\nown and is *not* a security boundary. If the port is reachable off your machine, put a reverse\nproxy or sidecar in front that owns authentication, and make sure the app port is not directly\nreachable. Binding a non-loopback address is fine and expected behind such a proxy."],[3148,"**Front it with an authenticating proxy if you expose it.** If the port is reachable on a shared\nor untrusted network, put a reverse proxy or sidecar in front that owns request authentication,\nand ensure the app port is not directly reachable. FastSkill will not police the bind address for\nyou, and binding a non-loopback address is the normal, expected configuration behind such a proxy."],[2468,"**Gate metric options** (per case, then averaged across the split — see\nSetup):"],[2542,"**Gate metric**"],[718,"**Generates Skill ID**: Uses the current directory name as the skill ID"],[3054,"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."],[2915,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[2919,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[1283,"**git-marketplace**: Git repository with `marketplace.json` for skill discovery"],[331,"**Global lock**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\fastskill\\global-skills.lock` (Windows)"],[1362,"**Grid**: Human-readable columnar layout with the same fields as table"],[3055,"**HTTP registry**: an HTTP index and downloadable skill artifacts."],[1288,"**http-registry**: HTTP-based registry with flat skill index"],[2846,"**ID** → Second directory level (the package name, must not contain slashes, e.g., \"web-scraper\")"],[2768,"**If you omit `checks` from `optimize.toml` entirely, there is no grading signal at all**: with zero checks configured, every case's result list is empty, and an empty list scores `1.0` under every `gate_metric` (vacuously — \"zero required checks passed\" is trivially true). In that configuration every candidate patch looks perfect, so the gate has nothing meaningful to accept or reject on. Always configure `checks` for a real run."],[3043,"**Include all metadata**: Provide tags, capabilities, and author information"],[2798,"**Incremental index rebuilding.** A change-detection cache (`.fastskill/build-cache.json`) lets\nFastSkill\nre-embed only what actually changed, so keeping the index current is cheap."],[1932,"**Index for search**: `fastskill index rebuild` (requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`)."],[1931,"**Install from the manifest**: `fastskill project install`."],[862,"**Installs Skills**: Stages and commits each overlapping dependency closure as one recovery unit"],[752,"**Invalid IDs:**"],[738,"**Invalid versions:**"],[1363,"**JSON**: Machine-readable array with fields: id, scope, name, description, latest\\_version, published\\_at, and optionally versions array"],[647,"**Judge errors and excluded trials.** A trial whose judgment errored contributes nothing to a `judge_score` — not a zero — and is counted in `totals.judge_errors`. A trial a gated judge could not judge is counted in `totals.judge_excluded_trials`."],[622,"**Judges**"],[374,"**Keep FastSkill up to date** to get lock file improvements and bug fixes"],[3041,"**Keep it updated**: Regenerate `marketplace.json` when skills change"],[2795,"**Keyword fallback otherwise.** If no embedding provider is configured, semantic ranking silently\nskips and resolution falls back to keyword matching — the endpoint still returns results, it just\nranks them without embeddings."],[338,"**Kill the conflicting process**:"],[1196,"**Large repositories** (1000+ skills): 10-30 minutes"],[2866,"**links**: Reserved for future use"],[361,"**Linux/macOS**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock`"],[856,"**Loads Dependencies**: Reads `[dependencies]` section from `skill-project.toml`"],[2322,"**Loads the full `SKILL.md`** for relevant skills to get instructions and parameters —\nthe same content `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` prints."],[3057,"**Local catalog**: skill content and catalog metadata on disk."],[2797,"**Local vector index.** Skill embeddings are stored in a local SQLite vector index (path set by\n`index_path` under `[tool.fastskill.embedding]`), so resolution queries run against on-disk vectors\nwith no external service call at query time."],[1295,"**local**: Local filesystem path"],[855,"**Locates Project File**: Finds `skill-project.toml` at project root or walks up directory tree"],[2321,"**Matches task requirements** against each skill's `description` frontmatter."],[2332,"**MCP access** — register the FastSkill MCP server for tool-based access inside Cursor"],[1195,"**Medium repositories** (100 skills): 2-5 minutes"],[2860,"**name**: Skill identifier"],[1183,"**Network Issues**: Check internet connectivity"],[3128,"**Never commit plaintext tokens.** Keep them in your shell profile, CI secret store, or a secrets\nmanager. Commit `skill-project.toml`; keep the token value out of the repo."],[645,"**Not-observable checks.** A check whose evidence the backend cannot produce records `passed: false` for older readers. It is excluded rather than counted as a failure."],[2446,"**Note on `aggregate_group_size` and `gate_trials`:** unlike the other numeric fields, these two\nare not checked by `fastskill`'s own config validation. A `0` value parses fine and passes\n`fastskill optimization run`'s validation step, then fails once the training loop starts, as\n`OPTIMIZE_TRAINING_FAILED: TEXTGRAD_INVALID_CONFIG: gate_trials must be > 0` (or the\nequivalent for `aggregate_group_size`) — confirmed by running the binary with `gate_trials = 0`."],[2608,"**Note:** `best_skill.md` is the highest-scoring skill document seen across all accepted\nsteps — not necessarily the final step. If the last few steps were rejected, it reflects the\nbest earlier checkpoint. A run where nothing was accepted exports the seed document, with\nthe optimizer's protected-region markers added."],[2680,"**Note:** Resume uses the config stored *inside* the run directory, not your original config file. This ensures the run is reproducible regardless of changes you may have made to the config since starting."],[3019,"**Note**: `skill-project.toml` provides metadata support (id, version, description, author, tags, 